1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,533
In this video you will back up a save, restore it, find backups made with DBI, JKSV

2
00:00:05,533 --> 00:00:08,867
or Checkpoint, and sync them with a WebDAV server.

3
00:00:08,867 --> 00:00:10,867
Open Tools, Game Tools, Saves.

4
00:00:10,867 --> 00:00:15,200
There are three tabs: Installed Games, Deleted Games and Backups.

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,400
Switch between them with L and R.

6
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:22,800
Each game has a single tile covering its complete save bundle with colored badges

7
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:26,267
for actual save types (Account, Device, BCAT, etc.).

8
00:00:26,267 --> 00:00:29,400
The line under the header shows active filters.

9
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:33,733
To choose other users or types, press plus and open Save Options.

10
00:00:33,733 --> 00:00:35,733
Let's make a backup.

11
00:00:35,733 --> 00:00:38,600
Highlight a game, or select several with X.

12
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:40,933
Press A and choose "Create backup".

13
00:00:40,933 --> 00:00:42,933
Backup Options opens.

14
00:00:42,933 --> 00:00:48,467
Location is where the backup is written, by default the dumps folder on the microSD

15
00:00:48,467 --> 00:00:50,467
card.

16
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:54,867
"Choose Folder..." lets you pick another one, also on a USB drive.

17
00:00:54,867 --> 00:00:59,000
If the console has several users, tick whose saves to back up.

18
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,400
Then choose Start Backup at the top.

19
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:04,067
At the end you see "Backup successful!".

20
00:01:04,067 --> 00:01:06,067
Empty saves are skipped.

21
00:01:06,067 --> 00:01:11,667
The backup is in the dumps folder, in a subfolder named after the game and the date.

22
00:01:11,667 --> 00:01:15,800
It uses the same ZIP format as DBI, so DBI can restore it too.

23
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:19,133
Normal backup automatically skips unchanged saves.

24
00:01:19,133 --> 00:01:23,333
Kefir Hub checks only its own backups in the selected location.

25
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:25,333
Now the restore.

26
00:01:25,333 --> 00:01:27,533
Before you start, close the game.

27
00:01:27,533 --> 00:01:31,667
If MTP is running, turn it off, or the restore will not start.

28
00:01:31,667 --> 00:01:34,800
Highlight the game, press A and choose Restore.

29
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:37,933
In Restore Options, choose the backup location.

30
00:01:37,933 --> 00:01:41,467
Kefir Hub is selected when its backups are available.

31
00:01:41,467 --> 00:01:45,400
For another app's backups, explicitly select Backup Source.

32
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,400
Then choose Start Restore.

33
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:50,067
Kefir Hub asks which user gets the save.

34
00:01:50,067 --> 00:01:53,600
A backup of one user can be restored to another user.

35
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:56,200
If there are several backups, pick one.

36
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:59,800
The newest is at the top, each with its date and time.

37
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:02,000
Confirm the last window with Yes.

38
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:07,067
Before overwriting, Kefir Hub keeps the current save as a safety copy in the

39
00:02:07,067 --> 00:02:09,067
dumps/recovery folder.

40
00:02:09,067 --> 00:02:14,667
At the end you see "Restore successful!", and the window shows where the safety copy

41
00:02:14,667 --> 00:02:16,667
is.

42
00:02:16,667 --> 00:02:21,933
To undo the restore, open the Backups tab: in that game's "Kefir Hub" group the

43
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:24,067
safety copy is one more archive.

44
00:02:24,067 --> 00:02:26,067
Restore it from there.

45
00:02:26,067 --> 00:02:31,533
Its date is when the save was last written before the restore, so it may not be at

46
00:02:31,533 --> 00:02:33,533
the top.

47
00:02:33,533 --> 00:02:37,867
If the user has no save for this game yet, Kefir Hub creates one.

48
00:02:37,867 --> 00:02:42,600
This works for regular user saves, and only when the game is installed.

49
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:45,733
Device and BCAT saves are not created this way.

50
00:02:45,733 --> 00:02:49,133
For those, start the game once first, then restore.

51
00:02:49,133 --> 00:02:54,600
The Backups tab shows the backups on the microSD card made by Kefir Hub, DBI, JKSV

52
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:57,933
and Checkpoint, grouped by the app that made them.

53
00:02:57,933 --> 00:03:01,533
Kefir Hub looks in the standard folders of these apps.

54
00:03:01,533 --> 00:03:07,067
If your backups are somewhere else, add the folder in Settings, Saves, "Save Backup

55
00:03:07,067 --> 00:03:09,067
Search Paths".

56
00:03:09,067 --> 00:03:14,467
Each game has a tile for each backup source representing the complete save bundle

57
00:03:14,467 --> 00:03:16,467
for all users.

58
00:03:16,467 --> 00:03:20,800
Highlight it and press A to open actions for this game's backups.

59
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:24,467
To restore several games together, select tiles with X.

60
00:03:24,467 --> 00:03:28,867
Choose Restore and continue as before: user, backup, confirmation.

61
00:03:28,867 --> 00:03:33,467
In the same menu, "Verify integrity" checks the group's ZIP archives.

62
00:03:33,467 --> 00:03:37,867
"Delete older backups" keeps only the newest backup in each group.

63
00:03:37,867 --> 00:03:41,600
Backups on a USB drive do not appear on the Backups tab.

64
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:46,600
To restore one, start from the Installed Games tab and pick the drive under

65
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:48,600
Location.

66
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:53,067
Delete erases the save from the console and does not make a backup.

67
00:03:53,067 --> 00:03:55,400
Make a backup before you choose it.

68
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:58,400
You can also keep backups on a WebDAV server.

69
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:03,333
Add it in Settings, Saves, "Save sync location", "+ Add network location".

70
00:04:03,333 --> 00:04:07,267
Select the games, press plus and choose "Sync with remote".

71
00:04:07,267 --> 00:04:12,533
Backups missing on the server are uploaded, and backups missing on the card are

72
00:04:12,533 --> 00:04:14,533
downloaded.

73
00:04:14,533 --> 00:04:17,667
Files with the same name are never overwritten.

74
00:04:17,667 --> 00:04:21,533
On the server the backups are in the sphaira-saves folder.

75
00:04:21,533 --> 00:04:26,867
Downloaded backups are not applied by themselves; restore them as shown earlier.

76
00:04:26,867 --> 00:04:31,733
"Auto-sync after backup" uploads every new backup right after it is made.

77
00:04:31,733 --> 00:04:37,333
"Include remote backups" in Restore Options downloads the backups that exist only on

78
00:04:37,333 --> 00:04:39,400
the server before you pick one.

79
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:42,800
For more, read the Saves page in the documentation.
